That's the point: you simply don't like this type of game. I for example don't
like text adventures - but I acknowledge the fact that some people do love
them... Nethack is almost like two games, with gradual shift from one to 
another during playing. It starts as a simple-minded 'classic RPG' (similar
to old rogue or moria) - but then it shifts towards 'adventure' type game
- one where the main goal is not just staying alive, but solving puzzles
and generally 'collecing experience'.

Just look around - there are thousands of computer games. Pick one you like
and play it! Ever tried moria or omega? From your comments seems that you
could like those...
